§ `Article 31 as a whole: the answers of the paragraphs`

#ASSERT `Art 31 the notified body has satisfied the requirements given the answers of the paragraphs` (LIST (JUST TRUE), (JUST TRUE), (JUST TRUE)) EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 31 the notified body has satisfied the requirements given the answers of the paragraphs` (LIST (JUST TRUE), (JUST FALSE), (JUST TRUE)) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Art 31 the notified body has satisfied the requirements given the answers of the paragraphs` (LIST (JUST TRUE), NOTHING, (JUST TRUE)) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Art 31 the notified body has satisfied the requirements given the answers of the paragraphs` (LIST (JUST FALSE), NOTHING) EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Art 31 the notified body has satisfied the requirements given the answers of the paragraphs` (LIST NOTHING) EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Art 31 the notified body has satisfied the requirements given the answers of the paragraphs` EMPTY EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Article 32`

-- args: date asked, demonstrates conformity with the criteria of the relevant harmonised standards, references published in the Official Journal, the standards cover the requirement
#ASSERT `Art 32 the conformity assessment body is presumed to comply with the requirement set out in Article 31` (Date 2 8 2025) TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 32 the conformity assessment body is presumed to comply with the requirement set out in Article 31` (Date 2 8 2025) TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- RECONCILED 2026-11-17: was #ASSERT `Art 32 the conformity assessment body is presumed to comply with the requirement set out in Article 31` (Date 2 8 2025) TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING; the references have not been published, so the "Where" condition of Article 32 fails, and the periods ruling's rule (b) answers a failed "where" JUST FALSE (fork F-32-where)
#ASSERT `Art 32 the conformity assessment body is presumed to comply with the requirement set out in Article 31` (Date 2 8 2025) TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- RECONCILED 2026-11-17: was #ASSERT `Art 32 the conformity assessment body is presumed to comply with the requirement set out in Article 31` (Date 2 8 2025) FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING; the body does not demonstrate conformity with the criteria, so the "Where" condition of Article 32 fails, and the periods ruling's rule (b) answers a failed "where" JUST FALSE (fork F-32-where)
#ASSERT `Art 32 the conformity assessment body is presumed to comply with the requirement set out in Article 31` (Date 2 8 2025) FALSE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- The "Where" fails in both limbs, or in one limb while the standards do not cover the requirement: still the failed "where" (JUST FALSE); only a body that meets the "Where" and whose standards do not cover the requirement is outside the scope limit "in so far as" (NOTHING, above).
#ASSERT `Art 32 the conformity assessment body is presumed to comply with the requirement set out in Article 31` (Date 2 8 2025) FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Art 32 the conformity assessment body is presumed to comply with the requirement set out in Article 31` (Date 2 8 2025) TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Art 32 the conformity assessment body is presumed to comply with the requirement set out in Article 31` (Date 2 8 2025) FALSE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Art 32 the conformity assessment body is presumed to comply with the requirement set out in Article 31` (Date 1 8 2025) TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Art 32 the conformity assessment body is presumed to comply with the requirement set out in Article 31` (Date 1 12 2026) TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
